<title>USA: US firms to buy 536 mln lbs flue-cured tobacco.</title>
<headline>US firms to buy 536 mln lbs flue-cured tobacco.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cigarette makers reported they intend to buy 536 million lbs of 1997 crop flue-cured tobacco, the Agriculture Department said Monday.</p>
<p>Major domestic manufacturers are required by law to report their expected purchases of flue-cured tobacco. It is one of the factors used by USDA in setting the marketing quota for flue-cured tobacco.</p>
<p>The 1997 quota will be announced by December 16.</p>
<p>For 1996, manufacturers said they would buy 475.5 million lbs of U.S.-grown flue-cured tobacco.</p>
</text>
